Title: Auto-generate skills catalog in README.md from SKILL.md frontmatter
Created: 2026-05-14
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-05-14T15:06Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
## Context

Surfaced from 0153 design exploration (raid 2026-05-14). The 0153 exploration
concluded:
- Agent introspection mid-session is already solved by Claude Code's platform
  (system-reminder injects every skill's name+description on every turn)
- The actual gap is human-facing: README.md hand-lists 22 of 27 skills and
  is already drifting

Recommended approach: auto-generated skills catalog in README.md.

Rejected alternatives:
- /show-docs and /show-skill — redundant with platform-provided system-reminder
- Architecture page from ticket history — orthogonal to staleness
- Docs-as-source-of-truth — overkill for 27-skill personal harness
- Embedded query/RAG — over-engineering; `grep -r` suffices

## Actions

1. Add Makefile target `make skills-catalog`:
   - Read `description:` from frontmatter of every `skills/*/SKILL.md`
   - Regenerate the skills section in README.md between sentinel comments
     (e.g. `<!-- skills:begin -->` ... `<!-- skills:end -->`)
   - Sort alphabetically; group user-invocable separately from internal helpers
2. Add CI check that fails if `make skills-catalog` produces a diff
   (drift detection — catches forgotten regeneration before merge)
3. Run once locally to populate README.md sentinel block
4. Document in CLAUDE.md / contributing notes: regenerate after adding/renaming/
   removing a skill

## Notes

- Authoring detail: SKILL.md frontmatter sometimes has multi-line descriptions
  (e.g., schedule, claude-api). Use a YAML parser, not regex.
- Some entries (init, review, security-review) are built-in Claude Code skills,
  not present as SKILL.md — handle missing files gracefully

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `make skills-catalog` regenerates README.md skills section
- [ ] CI check fails if README.md is out of sync with skill frontmatter
- [ ] README.md updated to current state of skills/
